 What is OOM in Spark? Out Of Memory (OOM) 
=> An OOM (Out of Memory) error occurs when Spark tries to process more data than the executor or driver has memory for — 
   leading to the application crashing or failing with errors like:
   java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space
   java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: GC overhead limit exceeded
